  "caption": "Quinn's party trick has always been extra-bendy joints. Lately, though, those joints ache by evening and the ankles roll on flat ground.\n\nBeing bendy is usually harmless. It matters when it brings symptoms: looser ligaments give less passive support, so muscles have to do more of the work.\n\nWhat often helps: strength training in a controlled range, balance work so joints sense where they are, pacing to avoid boom-bust weeks, and skipping extreme end-range stretches. Yoga and Pilates can still fit, with a focus on control. Progress tends to build over months.\n\nGet it checked if you have frequent sprains or joints that slip out, pain in many joints, or fatigue that seems out of proportion.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
